# What the e2 composite-figure rules produce, in sha256sum format, paths relative to
# data/derived. e2_fig_composite_verify checks a build against it.
#
# The three JSON caches are plain data and match on any host that has E2's deposit AND the
# two trees panel (a) reads from outside it (config e2.e1_sweep, e2.e1_extra) -- depositing
# those is what makes this manifest checkable elsewhere.
#
# Nothing here is a function of anything but those inputs, which is what lets the manifest
# pass while the bands are still running: `composite-census.json` holds the fields that move
# with the host rather than with the figure (the finished table's write time and checksum,
# and which cells sit on disk unreported) and is deliberately absent from this file.
#
# The figure's bytes are matplotlib's, with the PDF's CreationDate and the PNG's Software
# stamp suppressed, so they match on a host with the same matplotlib as requirements.lock.
#
# Cut 2026-11-02 against the finished set of that day: 85 proteins screened for panel
# (a), 45 finished for panel (b), of which 27 are exact at every level and 24 have all
# three sets binding. The 45 are the finished set less eGFP and RBD, the two sequences in
# it that are not human proteins, excluded at every rung by `cellset` with the reason.
# Panel (a)'s 85 is the screen's own population and is not a function of the grid, so it
# does not move with that exclusion. The set moves as the grid closes cells, so a rebuild after an
# arrival will differ here and the pin is re-cut with the population it describes.
555a35e75bebba983f4d5168a7a411e50a2771c0c4859bd53812c89a0c8ff4ea  e2/composite/composite-data.json
e0af9092f7be6cc3e141b8fb1aaff762dd810c6535af384cea6eb2f896635429  e2/composite/dcai-at-mfe.json
03e0975191437c55b45ec88149fb63265cfd3f1c657386e7dbb5b7e18356537a  e2/composite/example-Q6PF06-c80-none.json
